  "title": "Hōne Heke",
  "summary": "Hōne Heke Pōkai was a Ngāpuhi leader of the Bay of Islands and the first chief to sign the Treaty of Waitangi in 1840. Angered at the loss of chiefly authority, he and his allies cut down the Kororāreka flagstaff in 1844–1845, the last time on 11 March 1845, opening the Northern War. He died in 1850.",
